James asked whether the correct format for ending a quote should present the author or document first. I clarified that the more common format is “Quote.” — **Author**, *Document*. For example, the quote by Martin Luther King Jr. was provided to illustrate this format. I noted that Document, Author is acceptable only if the document is emphasized or if required by a specific style guide. Additionally, I shared typography details, emphasizing the use of an em dash instead of two hyphens, italicizing titles of books/reports, putting article titles in quotation marks, and specifying formats for unknown authors. The recommended format was reiterated as — Author, *Document*.
